    "summary": "Oil painting on cotton cloth depicting Saint George slaying a dragon. Saint George is shown mounted on a richly carparisoned horse. The red saddle cloth, crupper, breastband, headgear and toe stirrup are all distinctly Ethiopian. He uses a long Ethiopian spear with a cross shaped finial to slay the dragon from whom a small blue devil appears. In the tree to the right is the maiden Biruwit, named here as Beruk.",
